IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eca-gateway`
IMPORT `eca-jurisdiction`

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 -- worked cases.
--
-- Claims about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The claim limits
-- are in regulations that were not retrieved, so every assertion about them uses
-- an explicitly invented pair of figures and says so.

§ `Fixtures -- claim limits`

-- THESE FIGURES ARE INVENTED. The real limits are prescribed under s 12(8)(e)
-- in regulations that were not read. They are here so the arithmetic in ss 12,
-- 14 and 15 can be exercised; nothing that depends on them is a statement about
-- Singapore law.
`an invented pair of claim limits` MEANS ClaimLimits WITH
    `the limit for contractual and statutory disputes under section 12(7)(a)` IS 20000
    `the limit for wrongful dismissal disputes under section 12(7)(b)` IS 20000

§ `Fixtures -- timing`

GIVEN `section 65 salary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `8A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `8B(7)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `84(2)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since last day` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since dismissal` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since confinement` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since earliest facts` IS A NUMBER,
      `months since these facts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A RequestTiming
DECIDE `timing` `section 65 salary` `8A(3)` `8B(7)` `14(2)` `84(2)` `ended` `months since last day` `months since dismissal` `months since confinement` `months since earliest facts` `months since these facts` IS
    RequestTiming WITH
        `the dispute is a recovery of salary under Employment Act section 65` IS `section 65 salary`
        `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8A(3)` IS `8A(3)`
        `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(7)` IS `8B(7)`
        `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 14(2)` IS `14(2)`
        `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 84(2)` IS `84(2)`
        `the employment relationship has ended` IS `ended`
        `months since the last day of employment` IS `months since last day`
        `months since the date of dismissal` IS `months since dismissal`
        `months since the date of confinement` IS `months since confinement`
        `months since the material facts giving rise to the earliest dispute listed` IS `months since earliest facts`
        `months since the material facts giving rise to this dispute` IS `months since these facts`
        `within the period allowed by Employment Act section 65(2A), as extended if it was` IS TRUE
        `within the time determined under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(8)` IS TRUE

-- s 3(2)(d): the central wrongful dismissal claim, one month from dismissal.
`dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 1 0 1 1
`dismissed six weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2 2 0 2 2

-- s 3(2)(e): the female employee's claim under Employment Act s 84(2), two
-- months from confinement.
`confined seven weeks ago, claim under 84(2)` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 2 2 2 2
`confined ten weeks ago, claim under 84(2)` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 3 3 3 3 3

-- s 3(2)(f): the employment has ended, six months from the last day.
`an unpaid allowance, left the job five months ago` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 5 0 0 5 5
`an unpaid allowance, left the job seven months ago` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 7 0 0 7 7

-- THE PAIR THAT MATTERS. Still employed, so limb (g) and one year from the
-- earliest dispute listed.
`an unpaid allowance from eleven months ago, still employed` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 11 11
`an unpaid allowance from thirteen months ago, still employed` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 13 13

-- And the case where limb (f) is satisfied and s 3(3)(a)(ii) is not: an
-- allowance unpaid eighteen months ago, and the employee resigned two months
-- ago after three years' service.
`an allowance unpaid eighteen months ago, left two months ago` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 2 0 0 18 18

-- s 3(2)(b): a re-employment dispute, six months from the last day.
`a re-employment dispute, left five months ago` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 5 0 0 5 5
`a re-employment dispute, left eight months ago` MEANS
    `timing` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 8 0 0 8 8

§ `Fixtures -- listing requirements`

GIVEN `has a money claim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the claim satisfies 12(2) to (4)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `facts within a year` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `already listed earlier` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribed requirements unmet` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `barred by section 16` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fee paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ListingRequirements
DECIDE `listing` `has a money claim` `the claim satisfies 12(2) to (4)` `facts within a year` `already listed earlier` `prescribed requirements unmet` `barred by section 16` `fee paid` IS
    ListingRequirements WITH
        `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS `has a money claim`
        `that claim satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4)` IS `the claim satisfies 12(2) to (4)`
        `the material facts occurred not earlier than one year before submission` IS `facts within a year`
        `the dispute is listed in an earlier accepted request not withdrawn before its first session` IS `already listed earlier`
        `an earlier accepted request was required to list the dispute and the prescribed requirements are not satisfied` IS `prescribed requirements unmet`
        `under section 16 the claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal` IS `barred by section 16`
        `the prescribed fee accompanied the request` IS `fee paid`

`an ordinary listable dispute` MEANS `listing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a dispute whose facts are over a year old` MEANS `listing` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a dispute already in an earlier accepted request` MEANS `listing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a dispute whose claim is barred by section 16` MEANS `listing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a listable dispute with no fee paid` MEANS `listing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 2 -- a dispute has to be about money`

#ASSERT `this is a specified employment dispute` `a specified contractual dispute`
#ASSERT `this is a specified employment dispute` `a specified statutory dispute`
#ASSERT `this is a specified employment dispute` `a wrongful dismissal dispute`

-- Both Schedule definitions are confined to "a dispute, relating to a payment of
-- an amount of money". A demotion, a transfer, a refused reference or a shift
-- roster is outside the tribunal however squarely it arises out of employment.
#ASSERT NOT `this is a specified employment dispute` `something else arising out of employment`

§ `Section 3(2) -- which limb governs, and the time it gives`

#ASSERT `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` EQUALS `limb (d) -- wrongful dismissal under section 14(2)`
#ASSERT `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `confined seven weeks ago, claim under 84(2)` EQUALS `limb (e) -- wrongful dismissal under section 84(2)`
#ASSERT `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `an unpaid allowance, left the job five months ago` EQUALS `limb (f) -- the employment relationship has ended`
#ASSERT `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `an unpaid allowance from eleven months ago, still employed` EQUALS `limb (g) -- anything else`
#ASSERT `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `a re-employment dispute, left five months ago` EQUALS `limb (b) -- re-employment under section 8A(3)`

-- One month from dismissal under limb (d). This is the shortest period in the
-- Act and it governs the claim most employees bring.
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)`
#ASSERT NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `dismissed six weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)`

-- Two months from confinement under limb (e).
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `confined seven weeks ago, claim under 84(2)`
#ASSERT NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `confined ten weeks ago, claim under 84(2)`

-- Six months from the last day under limb (f), and under limb (b).
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `an unpaid allowance, left the job five months ago`
#ASSERT NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `an unpaid allowance, left the job seven months ago`
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `a re-employment dispute, left five months ago`
#ASSERT NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `a re-employment dispute, left eight months ago`

-- One year from the earliest dispute listed, under limb (g).
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `an unpaid allowance from eleven months ago, still employed`
#ASSERT NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `an unpaid allowance from thirteen months ago, still employed`

§ `Section 3(3)(a)(ii) -- the second limitation period, and what it does to limb (f)`

#ASSERT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `an ordinary listable dispute`
#ASSERT NOT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `a dispute whose facts are over a year old`
#ASSERT NOT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `a dispute already in an earlier accepted request`
#ASSERT NOT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `a dispute whose claim is barred by section 16`

-- THE TRAP. s 3(2)(f) gives six months from the last day of employment, and the
-- employee who resigned two months ago is inside it. s 3(3)(a)(ii) requires the
-- material facts to be no earlier than one year before submission, and an
-- allowance unpaid eighteen months ago is outside that. Both are satisfied
-- separately; the dispute still cannot be listed.
#ASSERT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `an allowance unpaid eighteen months ago, left two months ago`
#ASSERT NOT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `a dispute whose facts are over a year old`

-- So the six-month window in limb (f) is in substance a one-year window from the
-- facts, whichever is shorter. The Commissioner has a ground to refuse the
-- request even though the request itself is in time.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` `an allowance unpaid eighteen months ago, left two months ago` `a dispute whose facts are over a year old` TRUE

-- s 3(4) is a power and not a duty, so a ground to refuse is not a refusal.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` `dismissed six weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` `an ordinary listable dispute` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` `dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` `a listable dispute with no fee paid` TRUE

-- s 3(4)(a)(ii) brings the claim limit forward into the gateway.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` `dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` `an ordinary listable dispute` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` `dismissed three weeks ago, wrongful dismissal under 14(2)` `an ordinary listable dispute` TRUE

-- s 3(5): once accepted, the referral is mandatory.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner must refer every listed dispute for mediation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Commissioner must refer every listed dispute for mediation` FALSE

§ `Section 6 -- the certificate, and who loses by not turning up`

GIVEN `respondent absent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no settlement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no prospect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `settled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claimant absent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `power exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MediationOutcome
DECIDE `outcome` `respondent absent` `no settlement` `no prospect` `settled` `withdrawn` `claimant absent` `power exercised` IS
    MediationOutcome WITH
        `the respondent was given reasonable notice and did not attend` IS `respondent absent`
        `no settlement was reached at the end of the mediation` IS `no settlement`
        `the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement` IS `no prospect`
        `the dispute was settled` IS `settled`
        `the dispute was withdrawn from the list` IS `withdrawn`
        `the claimant failed without reasonable excuse to attend a mediation session` IS `claimant absent`
        `the mediator exercised the section 6(3) power to refuse a certificate` IS `power exercised`

`the respondent did not turn up` MEANS `outcome` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`mediation held, no settlement` MEANS `outcome` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the mediator saw no prospect of settlement` MEANS `outcome` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the dispute settled` MEANS `outcome` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the claimant withdrew the dispute` MEANS `outcome` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`the claimant did not turn up, and was refused a certificate` MEANS `outcome` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`the claimant did not turn up, and was given one anyway` MEANS `outcome` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Each of the three s 6(2) grounds produces a certificate.
#ASSERT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the respondent did not turn up`
#ASSERT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `mediation held, no settlement`
#ASSERT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the mediator saw no prospect of settlement`

-- s 6(4): a settled or withdrawn dispute is not unresolved, so no certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `the dispute is unresolved within section 6(4)` `the dispute settled`
#ASSERT NOT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the dispute settled`
#ASSERT NOT `the dispute is unresolved within section 6(4)` `the claimant withdrew the dispute`
#ASSERT NOT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the claimant withdrew the dispute`

-- THE ASYMMETRY. A respondent who does not attend hands the claimant a
-- certificate under s 6(2)(a). A claimant who does not attend can be refused one
-- under s 6(3) -- and s 12(5) then means no claim can be lodged at all.
#ASSERT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the respondent did not turn up`
#ASSERT `the mediator may refuse a certificate under section 6(3)` `the claimant did not turn up, and was refused a certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the claimant did not turn up, and was refused a certificate`

-- The power is discretionary, so the same absence need not be fatal.
#ASSERT `the mediator may refuse a certificate under section 6(3)` `the claimant did not turn up, and was given one anyway`
#ASSERT `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` `the claimant did not turn up, and was given one anyway`

§ `Section 7 -- the claim limit binds a settlement too`

GIVEN `in form` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `within contractual limit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `within dismissal limit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Settlement
DECIDE `settlement` `in form` `signed` `within contractual limit` `within dismissal limit` `registered` IS
    Settlement WITH
        `a settlement agreement in the prescribed form was entered into` IS `in form`
        `it was signed by or on behalf of each party` IS `signed`
        `the total payable for contractual and statutory disputes is within the prescribed limit` IS `within contractual limit`
        `the total payable for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the prescribed limit` IS `within dismissal limit`
        `registered in a District Court` IS `registered`

`a settlement in order and registered` MEANS `settlement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a settlement in order but not registered` MEANS `settlement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a settlement above the contractual limit` MEANS `settlement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a settlement nobody signed` MEANS `settlement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the settlement complies with section 7(1)` `a settlement in order and registered`
#ASSERT `the settlement is enforceable as a District Court judgment` `a settlement in order and registered`
#ASSERT NOT `the settlement is enforceable as a District Court judgment` `a settlement in order but not registered`

-- s 7(1)(b) and (c) import the same claim limits as s 12(7). Parties who agree a
-- figure above the limit cannot record it in a settlement agreement under this
-- Part, and s 15's power to abandon the excess has no counterpart at mediation.
#ASSERT NOT `the settlement complies with section 7(1)` `a settlement above the contractual limit`
#ASSERT NOT `a party at a mediation may abandon an excess over the claim limit`
#ASSERT NOT `the settlement complies with section 7(1)` `a settlement nobody signed`

§ `Section 12 -- jurisdiction`

GIVEN `who` IS A ClaimantKind,
      `the kind` IS A DisputeKind,
      `the matter` IS A ScheduledMatter,
      `prescribed for (c)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `money` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `certificates` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in time after the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contractual total` IS A NUMBER,
      `dismissal total` IS A NUMBER,
      `abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Claim
DECIDE `a claim` `who` `the kind` `the matter` `prescribed for (c)(ii)` `money` `reinstatement` `certificates` `in time after the certificate` `contractual total` `dismissal total` `abandoned` IS
    Claim WITH
        `who is bringing it` IS `who`
        `the kind of dispute` IS `the kind`
        `the scheduled matter it concerns` IS `the matter`
        `the matter is one prescribed for section 12(2)(c)(ii)` IS `prescribed for (c)(ii)`
        `it claims one or more amounts alleged to be payable` IS `money`
        `it claims reinstatement` IS `reinstatement`
        `a claim referral certificate was issued for every dispute in the claim` IS `certificates`
        `lodged within the prescribed period after the certificate issued` IS `in time after the certificate`
        `the total for contractual and statutory disputes, in dollars` IS `contractual total`
        `the total for wrongful dismissal disputes, in dollars` IS `dismissal total`
        `the excess over a claim limit has been abandoned under section 15` IS `abandoned`

`an employee claiming unpaid overtime` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified statutory dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5000 0 FALSE

`an employee claiming reinstatement for wrongful dismissal` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a wrongful dismissal dispute` `no scheduled matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE

-- Reinstatement asked for on a contractual dispute. s 12(3)(b) ties it to a
-- wrongful dismissal dispute.
`an employee claiming reinstatement for unpaid overtime` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified statutory dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE

`an employer claiming salary in lieu of notice` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employer suing their employee` `a specified contractual dispute` `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 3000 0 FALSE

-- An employer claiming something else in the Schedules: unpaid training bond,
-- recorded as another Schedule matter.
`an employer claiming some other Schedule matter` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employer suing their employee` `a specified contractual dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 3000 0 FALSE

`an employee with no certificate` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified statutory dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 0 FALSE

`an employee who lodged too late after the certificate` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified statutory dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5000 0 FALSE

`an employee claiming a dispute that is not about money` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `something else arising out of employment` `no scheduled matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5000 0 FALSE

`an employee the regulations do not cover` MEANS
    `a claim` `someone the regulations do not prescribe` `a specified statutory dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5000 0 FALSE

-- Over the invented contractual limit of $20,000 by $5,000.
`an employee claiming $25,000 of unpaid wages` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified contractual dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 25000 0 FALSE

`the same claim, with the excess abandoned` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a specified contractual dispute` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 25000 0 TRUE

-- Both kinds at once, each measured against its own limit. $18,000 of wages and
-- $25,000 of wrongful dismissal: inside one limit, outside the other.
`a mixed claim, inside one limit and outside the other` MEANS
    `a claim` `a prescribed employee suing their employer` `a wrongful dismissal dispute` `no scheduled matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 18000 25000 FALSE

#ASSERT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee claiming unpaid overtime` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee claiming reinstatement for wrongful dismissal` `an invented pair of claim limits`

-- s 12(3)(b): reinstatement is the Act's only non-money remedy and it belongs to
-- a wrongful dismissal dispute alone.
#ASSERT `section 12(3) is satisfied` `an employee claiming reinstatement for wrongful dismissal`
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(3) is satisfied` `an employee claiming reinstatement for unpaid overtime`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee claiming reinstatement for unpaid overtime` `an invented pair of claim limits`

-- s 12(2)(c): the employer's access to the tribunal is three Schedule items and
-- whatever else is prescribed. Nothing else.
#ASSERT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination`
#ASSERT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `Second Schedule item 14 -- the employer's entitlement under Employment Act section 11(1)`
#ASSERT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `Second Schedule item 16 -- the employer's entitlement under Employment Act section 16`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `Second Schedule item 13 -- the employee's entitlement under Employment Act section 11(1)`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `Second Schedule item 15 -- the employee's entitlement under Employment Act section 16`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a matter section 12(2)(c)(i) names` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule`

#ASSERT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employer claiming salary in lieu of notice` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2) is satisfied` `an employer claiming some other Schedule matter`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employer claiming some other Schedule matter` `an invented pair of claim limits`

-- The employee may claim any Schedule matter; the employer may not.
#ASSERT `section 12(2) is satisfied` `an employee claiming unpaid overtime`

-- s 12(5) and (6): the certificate, and the unstated period for lodging after it.
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee with no certificate` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee who lodged too late after the certificate` `an invented pair of claim limits`

#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee claiming a dispute that is not about money` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee the regulations do not cover` `an invented pair of claim limits`

-- s 12(1)'s closing words.
#ASSERT NOT `jurisdiction depends on whether the dispute arose before 1 April 2017`

§ `Sections 14 and 15 -- the excess, and what abandoning it costs`

-- The figures below depend on the INVENTED limits above.
#ASSERT `the contractual and statutory total exceeds its limit` `an employee claiming $25,000 of unpaid wages` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(7) is satisfied` `an employee claiming $25,000 of unpaid wages` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `an employee claiming $25,000 of unpaid wages` `an invented pair of claim limits`

-- s 15(2)(a) and (b): abandoning the excess deems s 12(7) satisfied and gives
-- the tribunal jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `section 12(7) is satisfied` `the same claim, with the excess abandoned` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT `the tribunal has jurisdiction` `the same claim, with the excess abandoned` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT `the amount abandoned if the claimant abandons the excess` `an employee claiming $25,000 of unpaid wages` `an invented pair of claim limits` EQUALS 5000

-- s 15(3): and the $5,000 is gone everywhere, not just here.
#ASSERT NOT `the abandoned amount can be recovered somewhere else` `the same claim, with the excess abandoned`

-- s 12(7) counts the two caps separately, so a claim can be inside one and
-- outside the other, and only the second needs abandoning down.
#ASSERT NOT `the contractual and statutory total exceeds its limit` `a mixed claim, inside one limit and outside the other` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT `the wrongful dismissal total exceeds its limit` `a mixed claim, inside one limit and outside the other` `an invented pair of claim limits`
#ASSERT `the amount abandoned if the claimant abandons the excess` `a mixed claim, inside one limit and outside the other` `an invented pair of claim limits` EQUALS 5000

§ `Section 16(1) and (2) -- one forum`

GIVEN `pending elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `determined elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `section 119 claim pending` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Commissioner decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN OtherProceedings
DECIDE `other proceedings` `pending elsewhere` `determined elsewhere` `section 119 claim pending` `Commissioner decided` IS
    OtherProceedings WITH
        `proceedings relating to the claim are pending in another court or the Industrial Arbitration Court` IS `pending elsewhere`
        `proceedings relating to the claim have been heard and determined elsewhere` IS `determined elsewhere`
        `a claim under Employment Act section 119 in respect of the dispute is pending` IS `section 119 claim pending`
        `the Commissioner has inquired into and decided the dispute under Employment Act section 115` IS `Commissioner decided`

`nothing anywhere else` MEANS `other proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a District Court action already on foot` MEANS `other proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a District Court action already decided` MEANS `other proceedings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`the Commissioner has already decided it under section 115` MEANS `other proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`an Employment Act section 119 claim pending` MEANS `other proceedings` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) bars the claim` `nothing anywhere else`
#ASSERT `section 16(1) bars the claim` `a District Court action already on foot`
#ASSERT `section 16(1) bars the claim` `a District Court action already decided`
#ASSERT `section 16(1) bars the claim` `the Commissioner has already decided it under section 115`
#ASSERT `section 16(1) bars the claim` `an Employment Act section 119 claim pending`

-- s 16(2) bars the other forum while the tribunal claim is live, and lifts on
-- withdrawal, discontinuance or dismissal for want of jurisdiction. s 16(1)(a)
-- has no such lifting clause for a claim already "heard and determined".
#ASSERT `section 16(2) bars proceedings elsewhere` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(2) bars proceedings elsewhere` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(2) bars proceedings elsewhere` FALSE FALSE

§ `THE ORDER TRAP -- section 16(3) and (5) against section 16(4) and (6)`

GIVEN `dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `IRA 35(3)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `RRA 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `withdrew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Minister decided` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `after lodging` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Representations
DECIDE `representations` `dismissed` `IRA 35(3)` `RRA 8(1)` `withdrew` `Minister decided` `after lodging` IS
    Representations WITH
        `the employee was dismissed` IS `dismissed`
        `representations in writing have been made to the Minister under Industrial Relations Act section 35(3)` IS `IRA 35(3)`
        `representations in writing have been made to the Minister under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8(1)` IS `RRA 8(1)`
        `the employee withdrew those representations` IS `withdrew`
        `the Minister concerned has made a decision on those representations` IS `Minister decided`
        `the representations were made after the claim was lodged` IS `after lodging`

`no representations at all` MEANS `representations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Representations first, not withdrawn.
`representations made first and left standing` MEANS `representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Representations first, withdrawn before the Minister decided. The bar lifts.
`representations made first and withdrawn in time` MEANS `representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Representations first, withdrawn but the Minister had already decided.
`representations made first, withdrawn after a decision` MEANS `representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- Claim first, then representations. s 16(6) deems it discontinued.
`claim lodged first, then representations` MEANS `representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Claim first, then representations, then withdrawal. Nothing revives the claim.
`claim lodged first, representations made and then withdrawn` MEANS `representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `section 16(5) bars lodging a wrongful dismissal claim` `no representations at all`
#ASSERT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `no representations at all`

-- REPRESENTATIONS FIRST. The bar is conditional on limb (b), and limb (b) fails
-- if the employee withdraws before the Minister decides. So this order is
-- recoverable.
#ASSERT `section 16(5) bars lodging a wrongful dismissal claim` `representations made first and left standing`
#ASSERT NOT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `representations made first and left standing`

#ASSERT NOT `the condition in paragraph (b) is satisfied` `representations made first and withdrawn in time`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(5) bars lodging a wrongful dismissal claim` `representations made first and withdrawn in time`
#ASSERT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `representations made first and withdrawn in time`

-- Unless the Minister got there first.
#ASSERT `the condition in paragraph (b) is satisfied` `representations made first, withdrawn after a decision`
#ASSERT `section 16(5) bars lodging a wrongful dismissal claim` `representations made first, withdrawn after a decision`

-- CLAIM FIRST. s 16(6) deems the claim discontinued from the date of the
-- representations, and neither s 16(6) nor s 16(4) contains anything that
-- revives it. Withdrawing the representations changes nothing.
#ASSERT `section 16(6) deems a wrongful dismissal claim discontinued` `claim lodged first, then representations`
#ASSERT NOT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `claim lodged first, then representations`
#ASSERT `section 16(6) deems a wrongful dismissal claim discontinued` `claim lodged first, representations made and then withdrawn`
#ASSERT NOT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `claim lodged first, representations made and then withdrawn`

-- The two orders side by side: identical conduct, identical withdrawal, and only
-- one of them leaves a live claim.
#ASSERT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `representations made first and withdrawn in time`
#ASSERT NOT `a wrongful dismissal claim can still be pursued` `claim lodged first, representations made and then withdrawn`

-- s 16(3) and (4) do the same for the three named Schedule matters, and only
-- those three.
#ASSERT `section 16(3) bars lodging this claim` `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination` `representations made first and left standing`
#ASSERT `section 16(3) bars lodging this claim` `Second Schedule item 13 -- the employee's entitlement under Employment Act section 11(1)` `representations made first and left standing`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(3) bars lodging this claim` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` `representations made first and left standing`
#ASSERT `section 16(4) deems the claim discontinued` `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination` `claim lodged first, then representations`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(4) deems the claim discontinued` `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule` `claim lodged first, then representations`

-- s 16(3) also catches representations under the Retirement and Re-employment
-- Act; s 16(5) catches only the Industrial Relations Act route.
#ASSERT `section 16(3) bars lodging this claim` `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination` (`representations` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(5) bars lodging a wrongful dismissal claim` (`representations` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 21 -- evidence`

#ASSERT `the tribunal may draw an adverse inference under section 21(2)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal may draw an adverse inference under section 21(2)` FALSE

-- "May draw any inferences that the tribunal thinks fit" is a power, not a
-- presumption, and the tribunal need not keep a record of the evidence.
#ASSERT NOT `section 21(2) creates a presumption against the party`
#ASSERT NOT `the tribunal must keep a record of the evidence`

§ `Section 23 -- appeal`

GIVEN `law` IS A BOOLEAN, `jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN, `facts` IS A BOOLEAN, `permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Appeal
DECIDE `an appeal` `law` `jurisdiction` `facts` `permission` IS
    Appeal WITH
        `the ground involves a question of law` IS `law`
        `the ground is that the claim was outside the tribunal's jurisdiction` IS `jurisdiction`
        `the ground is that the tribunal found the facts wrongly` IS `facts`
        `a District Court has given permission to appeal` IS `permission`

`a question of law, with permission` MEANS `an appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a question of law, permission refused` MEANS `an appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a jurisdiction point, with permission` MEANS `an appeal` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`the tribunal got the facts wrong, with permission` MEANS `an appeal` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` `a question of law, with permission`
#ASSERT `an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` `a jurisdiction point, with permission`

-- There is no appeal on the facts, with or without permission.
#ASSERT NOT `the ground is one section 23(1) allows` `the tribunal got the facts wrong, with permission`
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` `the tribunal got the facts wrong, with permission`

-- And the gate is unappealable: s 23(2) requires a District Court's permission,
-- and s 23(4)(a) makes the giving or refusing of it final.
#ASSERT `the ground is one section 23(1) allows` `a question of law, permission refused`
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` `a question of law, permission refused`
#ASSERT NOT `a refusal of permission to appeal can itself be appealed`

-- s 24(1): the order is enforceable while the appeal runs unless a court says
-- otherwise.
#ASSERT `the order may be enforced while the appeal is pending` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the order may be enforced while the appeal is pending` TRUE

§ `Section 27 -- who proves what`

GIVEN `denies the relationship` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `denies the statutory duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `summary dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claim under 14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dismissed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice states performance or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `section 84(1) circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claim under 84(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BurdenFacts
DECIDE `burden facts` `denies the relationship` `denies the statutory duty` `summary dismissal` `claim under 14(2)` `dismissed with notice` `notice states performance or misconduct` `section 84(1) circumstances` `claim under 84(2)` IS
    BurdenFacts WITH
        `the person alleges they are not the employer or employee of the claimant` IS `denies the relationship`
        `the person alleges they have no duty under one of the three named Acts` IS `denies the statutory duty`
        `the employee was dismissed without notice under Employment Act section 14(1)` IS `summary dismissal`
        `the employee lodged a claim under Employment Act section 14(2)` IS `claim under 14(2)`
        `the employee was dismissed with notice` IS `dismissed with notice`
        `the notice is or purports to be given on the ground of poor performance or misconduct` IS `notice states performance or misconduct`
        `a notice of dismissal was given to a female employee in the section 84(1) circumstances` IS `section 84(1) circumstances`
        `the female employee lodged a claim under Employment Act section 84(2)` IS `claim under 84(2)`

`the respondent says it was never the employer` MEANS `burden facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`summary dismissal, claim under 14(2)` MEANS `burden facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`notice given, reason stated as poor performance` MEANS `burden facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`notice given, no reason stated at all` MEANS `burden facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a maternity dismissal, claim under 84(2)` MEANS `burden facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- s 27(1): whoever says they are not the employer has to prove it.
#ASSERT `the person making the allegation bears the burden under section 27(1)` `the respondent says it was never the employer`
#ASSERT NOT `the person making the allegation bears the burden under section 27(1)` `summary dismissal, claim under 14(2)`

-- s 27(2)(a) and (c): the employer proves just cause or excuse, and sufficient
-- cause.
#ASSERT `the employer bears the burden on the reason for the dismissal` `summary dismissal, claim under 14(2)`
#ASSERT `the employer bears the burden on the reason for the dismissal` `a maternity dismissal, claim under 84(2)`

-- s 27(2)(b) IS CONDITIONAL ON THE EMPLOYER HAVING STATED A REASON. An employer
-- who gives contractual notice and says "poor performance" takes on the burden
-- of proving poor performance. An employer who gives the same notice and says
-- nothing does not. The subsection rewards silence.
#ASSERT `the employer bears the burden on the reason for the dismissal` `notice given, reason stated as poor performance`
#ASSERT NOT `the employer bears the burden on the reason for the dismissal` `notice given, no reason stated at all`

§ `Section 28 -- contracting out`

GIVEN `excludes jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prevents a mediation request` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prevents a claim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made before 1 April 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AgreementTerm
DECIDE `a term` `excludes jurisdiction` `prevents a mediation request` `prevents a claim` `made before 1 April 2017` IS
    AgreementTerm WITH
        `purports to exclude or limit the jurisdiction of a tribunal` IS `excludes jurisdiction`
        `purports to prevent a person from submitting a mediation request` IS `prevents a mediation request`
        `purports to prevent a person from making a claim, application or appeal under this Act` IS `prevents a claim`
        `the agreement was made before 1 April 2017` IS `made before 1 April 2017`

`an arbitration clause in a 2015 contract` MEANS `a term` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a settlement barring any future claim` MEANS `a term` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a term requiring disputes to go to a foreign court` MEANS `a term` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an ordinary confidentiality clause` MEANS `a term` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the term is void under section 28` `an arbitration clause in a 2015 contract`
#ASSERT `the term is void under section 28` `a settlement barring any future claim`
#ASSERT `the term is void under section 28` `a term requiring disputes to go to a foreign court`
#ASSERT NOT `the term is void under section 28` `an ordinary confidentiality clause`

-- s 28 reaches an agreement "whether made before, on or after 1 April 2017".
#ASSERT NOT `the date of the agreement makes any difference under section 28`
